#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078136 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "31a9b20e-d159-5ff2-94dc-54b8d7b8e620" :question/math-academy-id "e-21785" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078256 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "91e7f8e9-dc03-5203-9d33-0175960ba276" :question/math-academy-id "e-6570" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078257 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "0fba12b1-fa78-5ff2-88e4-2a690105d321" :question/math-academy-id "e-6571" :question/problem "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2952d5cd-c942-5002-9d74-31df17954f4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375309} {:answer/id #uuid "c7cf81f4-8be0-5733-93bd-f0ee2352a580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375310} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8c0141-11a9-5c36-8ad5-c4912b447626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375311} {:answer/id #uuid "f435919c-886a-5ebf-9a0f-ce1e9c538e55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375312} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab6474e-210d-553d-86c3-ae6ef1de9062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce8c0141-11a9-5c36-8ad5-c4912b447626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375311} :answer-field/id #uuid "5838ff18-dac6-5a7e-ae4c-a12d2862eec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8616e65f-08e1-5256-9739-a39cfbef8685" :question/math-academy-id "q-130082" :question/problem "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{2}-2x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=1,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}-2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-2)+(2x-2) \\\\  & =2x+2x-2 \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51cb1566-700c-52dc-90b8-9dcdf0b15afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375316} {:answer/id #uuid "88902212-2250-544c-915e-ca37c1e5bb31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375317} {:answer/id #uuid "1570845c-a664-5c62-b105-7c6703d36d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375318} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ff9f13-8a36-5f56-9f83-aba9af9b158a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375319} {:answer/id #uuid "775fc221-4df7-5a71-b639-95e2da31b4dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "775fc221-4df7-5a71-b639-95e2da31b4dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375320} :answer-field/id #uuid "b022f572-42ec-551a-a14e-c7a590c3bd77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b28ba552-0720-523c-a07f-ee0dc4920daa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130245" :question/problem "Given that $D=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={e}^{-x}+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{3}=2,{a}_{2}=0,{a}_{1}=-3,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}+2) \\\\  & =(2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})({e}^{-x}+2) \\\\  & =2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{-x}+2)-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x}+2) \\\\  & =2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(-{e}^{-x})-3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+3{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x}+3{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f827385-78b8-5074-abc7-072244379424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375323} {:answer/id #uuid "0bdbec80-1f0a-592f-9945-c3c373030cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375324} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ec9ebc-c7e5-5d15-a052-83542cf70dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375325} {:answer/id #uuid "1bf8a170-d6c9-5c27-83b9-59323277b984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375326} {:answer/id #uuid "84ae7a16-6e9a-569e-9496-f3db32633a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0ec9ebc-c7e5-5d15-a052-83542cf70dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375325} :answer-field/id #uuid "81214fda-192d-516c-a355-68e6587cfd45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "176ec5e1-5571-58a7-aa73-8c65d654e715" :question/math-academy-id "q-130252" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={sin}^{2}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{3}=1,{a}_{2}=0,{a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}){sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({sin}^{2}⁡x)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({sin}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+2\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354dd450-d6cc-57c6-bb4d-861dca902542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375330} {:answer/id #uuid "194c681c-c646-5a66-8458-bc73573429b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375331} {:answer/id #uuid "0c19ca43-92a5-5bde-b5b0-5c681b0e6edf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375332} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5796e3-a93d-57e1-b325-f061cabd98e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375333} {:answer/id #uuid "c9af11ee-630b-5742-a055-da9f96232364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "354dd450-d6cc-57c6-bb4d-861dca902542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375330} :answer-field/id #uuid "be010712-22a5-5797-aeea-5fca9a4fab9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae8e11f9-76ee-5136-84f5-ee2730fadd95" :question/math-academy-id "q-337831" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{0}=-5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))-5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+2\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f92d7cc5-88b6-5b6a-ba28-d2ed21f25774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375337} {:answer/id #uuid "96d7e146-e783-578c-8133-398f16746015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375338} {:answer/id #uuid "6c79d7f3-5781-533a-b0e3-6f1fdf21285f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375339} {:answer/id #uuid "b062f595-1a20-5ad7-ad14-2151c0cacc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375340} {:answer/id #uuid "98ae471c-a779-5743-8dc8-9770e1901df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b062f595-1a20-5ad7-ad14-2151c0cacc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375340} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd24fa5a-d621-536f-bea9-7427d8a79fb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9da44061-75cb-556f-b5b9-b8feb953b691" :question/math-academy-id "q-337833" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+1,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=5,$ and ${a}_{0}=1.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))+1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+5\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39ebd7fe-94dc-5ed5-b467-b482447fd71e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375344} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac74c9f-3218-528a-9004-b36fe07e7ab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375345} {:answer/id #uuid "28ac6538-ea47-5a24-9c99-191a9df89709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375346} {:answer/id #uuid "65d6b453-e27d-5101-9a92-e394a845b556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375347} {:answer/id #uuid "067d4a2d-dd13-518b-8dc3-ab29eb9eeaaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+6x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39ebd7fe-94dc-5ed5-b467-b482447fd71e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375344} :answer-field/id #uuid "173ee987-de08-5249-b8e6-d86335481597" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20114241-062d-543a-9f4f-ce748afabc7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-337840" :question/problem "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+2,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{2}-1?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}={x}^{2},{f}_{1}=3,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+2)({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}-1)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-1)+2({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)+3(2x)+2({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2+6x+2{x}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+6x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3c11fd-07c1-5251-a07e-1be4bb3ce249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375351} {:answer/id #uuid "10962b55-a22f-5722-a86e-b12a18067958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375352} {:answer/id #uuid "50f3008b-81ea-5fa2-9660-7c95f2cffa54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375353} {:answer/id #uuid "d64bd750-7126-5a11-870b-adf87d8d8488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375354} {:answer/id #uuid "d3dbb1bd-6a1f-5b5f-b9fc-400e54c3228c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50f3008b-81ea-5fa2-9660-7c95f2cffa54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375353} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78f2d8b-5cbc-51a4-b2ef-c819e6b55f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e179d6c-08e2-5aee-afa9-4910eabac925" :question/math-academy-id "q-337843" :question/problem "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-3,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\frac{1}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=2x,$ and ${f}_{0}=-3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-3)\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+2x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-\\frac{3}{x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{3}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{5}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a5a232e-a789-527f-85c5-425e994be4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)(7-2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375358} {:answer/id #uuid "4317f84e-faf3-575d-b16c-15ee6cab87d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)(2{x}^{2}-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375359} {:answer/id #uuid "682e03e4-17c9-57f4-acdd-544faeaad16e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)(5-2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375360} {:answer/id #uuid "863e9f47-6fa3-510b-91e4-06f6323bed24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)(7-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375361} {:answer/id #uuid "223dfda0-35ad-5c39-8074-0f7b04fa46bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)(7+2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a5a232e-a789-527f-85c5-425e994be4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)(7-2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375358} :answer-field/id #uuid "675e46a1-6bdf-5bc0-a6b1-38954a9f8823" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c2ef7fa-df26-5470-9ade-ea40c942ab20" :question/math-academy-id "q-337848" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y,$ then $D({x}^{2}+1)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=5.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{2}+1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{2}+1) & =({x}^{2}+1)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}+1)-x({x}^{2}+1)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1)+5({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+1)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-x({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2x+5({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2-2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+1)+5({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+1)-2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+1)+5({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =7({x}^{2}+1)-2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+1)(7-2{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cc59f6-f157-5749-afe3-93060045914b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375365} {:answer/id #uuid "97743439-c804-5abd-b5a9-fd876471a86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{e}^{4x}(1-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375366} {:answer/id #uuid "f461ed0d-5338-57af-9c6c-974c364240f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375367} {:answer/id #uuid "18874d9b-e489-58c0-a89d-2898bb4302d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375368} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1bedfe-e208-5abc-b870-3bb2111130ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f461ed0d-5338-57af-9c6c-974c364240f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375367} :answer-field/id #uuid "905bc035-1cc9-55fa-b108-7047bee5f131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dcfd6c91-01b7-50b3-bad5-202e991e6987" :question/math-academy-id "q-337972" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{y}^{2},$ then $D({e}^{-2x})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=2y,$ and ${f}_{0}=3y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={e}^{-2x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{-2x}) & ={e}^{-2x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-2x})+2({e}^{-2x})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-2x})+3{({e}^{-2x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{-2x})+2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (-2{e}^{-2x})+3{e}^{-4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot 4{e}^{-2x}-4{e}^{-4x}+3{e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{-4x}-4{e}^{-4x}+3{e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a7ff2b-db94-5e5e-a0e3-48ac17a063a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375372} {:answer/id #uuid "4ba7e8c3-09ef-5bae-bd3a-2ce790790c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375373} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e3fabf-80cc-51df-8eff-2a188a6ce264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375374} {:answer/id #uuid "f44ceaee-1a0b-540f-aa9f-18f125340cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375375} {:answer/id #uuid "820dd39f-8642-5d66-a239-8b2dc44b0c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f44ceaee-1a0b-540f-aa9f-18f125340cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375375} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c788fbe-78f4-5b9d-8284-0696002e1f41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "089313bf-aa19-5bee-bec7-d3a2e00b66aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-337983" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4{y}^{2},$ then $D(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=4y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+4{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+4{cos}^{2}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+4{cos}^{2}⁡2x \\\\  & =-4{cos}^{2}⁡2x+4{cos}^{2}⁡2x \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88e85596-2d61-5894-bb45-6e4b495704eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5+4{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375379} {:answer/id #uuid "d60cd5f6-a03d-5d72-8962-9483d11d44d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5-2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375380} {:answer/id #uuid "809d361f-6bbd-5fbd-a257-e8a285392d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5+2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375381} {:answer/id #uuid "8c0974e0-dc6b-55e3-b0cf-10dbd97c8a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(-5-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375382} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3885a3-32aa-5183-afda-538af85850ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5+2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "809d361f-6bbd-5fbd-a257-e8a285392d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5+2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375381} :answer-field/id #uuid "16fe5a02-fa89-5de2-a248-1990411a8c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1bdbb3c-0c65-5920-a3cb-125d513ba1ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-338186" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-2xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y,$ then $D({x}^{3}+1)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=y,{f}_{1}=-2xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=4.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{3}+1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{3}+1) & =({x}^{3}+1)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{3}+1)-2x({x}^{3}+1)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}+1)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{x}^{2})-2x({x}^{3}+1)\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}+1)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)-6{x}^{3}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}+1)\\cdot 6-6{x}^{3}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =6({x}^{3}+1)-6{x}^{3}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =10+4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{6} \\\\  & =2(5+2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5936ad5d-47c1-54c8-b496-760a09fa8130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(6-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297574} {:answer/id #uuid "c93b093d-82c3-5b47-8a9a-c34b0321dc69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3+8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297575} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8641b5-6ade-5521-b3db-ca0bab88c272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297576} {:answer/id #uuid "a238c216-92e1-53f5-b4d6-87d88a93a1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0584f1-0aae-50ac-b6e5-640ece58a243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a238c216-92e1-53f5-b4d6-87d88a93a1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577} :answer-field/id #uuid "bde7448d-6255-54c0-936b-fe929ae4a8c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9314e42-73f2-5134-b5e1-c3785c0ac3fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-338254" :question/problem "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+3y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot (-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbc24d20-915b-559d-86ce-708c71d0bba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077692} {:answer/id #uuid "cf16255a-ddad-5299-81f1-e226592fb7c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077693} {:answer/id #uuid "e12ff0ed-3fe9-5355-b6cc-3fddb4eb1a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077694} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2728ba-7729-53fa-b48f-9bbfbd9b8e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077695} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd7d633-326f-576c-b2e8-b1929af9e5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd7d633-326f-576c-b2e8-b1929af9e5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077696} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc087144-2dd5-55ce-8a0c-b876c78dc2b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aafa2f72-0c71-525f-aadf-225190142a79" :question/math-academy-id "q-65037" :question/problem "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=2,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ce00ee8-937b-5f20-a6e3-d21130db359c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375386} {:answer/id #uuid "992e8b5e-a87d-5bea-9202-002881c0e20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375387} {:answer/id #uuid "079ccabc-bf6b-5fdd-a8e5-818af64f65bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375388} {:answer/id #uuid "66a36f27-0d45-5d19-889e-b062b351b528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375389} {:answer/id #uuid "133ff577-7ccc-5218-8a8d-19c32d1e8553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ce00ee8-937b-5f20-a6e3-d21130db359c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375386} :answer-field/id #uuid "64f7fd70-b843-53d1-b628-88970efb83be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2d18a34-5a8f-51af-9b4a-6e6117d9487f" :question/math-academy-id "q-91033" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=-2,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e34cdc8-3a94-5e8f-bee6-3347fb11de3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375393} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2dc3a4-99f3-5c1c-9a9d-49644d6874a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375394} {:answer/id #uuid "45261384-aa34-5ceb-849a-2e8b2385a3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375395} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d080cc-bf02-561f-9de6-ab2cdd8bc2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375396} {:answer/id #uuid "04e9bfc1-bc8c-5f52-8cf4-f98b0461fd59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d2dc3a4-99f3-5c1c-9a9d-49644d6874a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375394} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a773db-6736-54e2-917c-021730e82401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18c0f2b0-ff21-5f76-aade-4d915d487306" :question/math-academy-id "q-91045" :question/problem "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}={x}^{2},{f}_{2}=-2x,{f}_{1}=x,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{4}) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}){x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{4})-2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{4})+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(4{x}^{3})-2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{3})+x(4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12{x}^{2})-2x(12{x}^{2})+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(24x)-24{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & =24{x}^{3}-24{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & =4{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
